{title: Smoldering Stubs of Firewood}
{subtitle: 2 Kings 15:25–27; Isaiah 7:1–4; 2 Kings 16:5–7; 15:29; 15:30–31}
{key: Bb}
{tempo: 74}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Bb] | [Bb] | [Gm] | [Eb] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
Pekah son of Re[Bb]maliah rose
Fifty men [Gm]of Gilead close
In Sa[Eb]maria’s royal seat
The [F]king of Israel’s de[Eb]feat
He killed the [F]man he served
To [Bb]take the [F/A]crown he de[Gm]served
Reigned for [Eb]twenty years long
In the [F]days of Israel’s song
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Be careful, keep [Bb]calm, do not be af[Gm]raid
Do not lose [Eb]heart over the anger dis[F]played
Two smoldering [Bb]stubs of firewood [Gm]burn
While the [Eb]kings of the [F]north and south [Bb]turn
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
Rezin of Aram marched up
Against Jeru[Gm]salem’s cup
They [Eb]laid siege but could not prevail
The heart [F]shook like a tree in the gale
[Eb]Word came to Da[F]vid’s house
A[Bb]ram joined [F/A]the north[Gm]ern cause
[Eb]Ahaz sent messengers a[F]way
To Tig-lath-Pi-le-ser’s day
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Be careful, [Bb]keep calm, do not be af[Gm]raid
Do not lose [Eb]heart over the anger dis[F]played
Two smoldering [Bb]stubs of firewood [Gm]burn
While the [Eb]kings of the [F]north and south [Bb]turn
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
[Gm]Tig-lath-Pi-le-ser [F]came strong
Capturing [Eb]Ijon and Abel Beth Maacah along
[Gm]Deporting the people [F]far away
To [Eb]Assyria’s end of day
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
Hoshea son of [Bb]Elah conspired
Killed the [Gm]king who aspired
Became [Eb]king in his place
In the [F]twenty year’s grace
{end_of_verse}

{comment: Outro (instrumental)}
